1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,952
Chapter seventeen — process capability.

2
00:00:04,012 --> 00:00:11,764
Switch to swimlanes and the
organization becomes the work it does.

3
00:00:11,824 --> 00:00:20,678
Lanes are roles. Cards are
steps. Arrows are handoffs.

4
00:00:20,738 --> 00:00:32,876
Cycle time: one point three days — three
hours of work, and a day and a bit of waiting.

5
00:00:32,936 --> 00:00:45,068
Flow efficiency: nine per cent. Typical is
five to fifteen. Almost all of it is queue.

6
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:54,367
Five handoffs, and every
one of them crosses a lane.

7
00:00:54,427 --> 00:01:06,063
Rolled yield: fifty-nine per cent. Forty-one
per cent of this process is rework.

8
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:16,568
Which is one point seven sigma — four
hundred and ten thousand defects per million.

9
00:01:16,628 --> 00:01:28,077
Computed from first-pass yield through the normal
curve, with the conventional one point five sigma shift.

10
00:01:28,137 --> 00:01:36,087
And it names the worst step,
so you know where to start.

11
00:01:36,147 --> 00:01:40,543
Open that step and the same
maths is there, per step.

12
00:01:40,603 --> 00:01:50,551
Work, wait, first-pass yield — and the
sigma and DPMO that fall out of them.

13
00:01:50,611 --> 00:02:00,561
Plus who is accountable, who contributes,
and what those people cost per month.

14
00:02:00,621 --> 00:02:07,126
Six Sigma without a spreadsheet,
on the process as modelled.
